// Gobra contracts for MemStore — F3, F5 (Go scope), F6, F9.
//
// F5 caveat: the mutex specs below establish data-race freedom under partial
// correctness. They do NOT prove deadlock-freedom or starvation-freedom.
// Those are explicitly out of scope and tested instead via `go test -race`
// in CI's race job.
//
// Stream 3 Phase 4 sub-PR (PutUser): introduces the `LockP()` permission
// predicate over `*MemStore`. Same shape as `internal/clock/clock.gobra`
// (S3P1a) and `internal/ids/ids.gobra` (S3P2a): the predicate abstracts the
// resource the `mu` mutex protects (write permission to `users`, `follows`,
// and `byAuthor`). `New()` folds the predicate after construction. The first
// production method to consume it is `PutUser`, which now carries an in-line
// `requires acc(s.LockP())` / `ensures acc(s.LockP())` contract instead of
// `// @ trusted` — so the F3 / F6 / F9 ghost stubs for the remaining store
// methods (PutFollow / DeleteFollow / PutTweet / FollowSet / HomeTimeline)
// below stay in place until the follow-up sub-PRs in this stream lift them.
//
// Stream 3 Phase 4 sub-PR 2 (HasUser): retires the `GhostHasUser` ghost stub
// — `(*MemStore).HasUser` is now its own proof in `memstore.go`, with the
// same `LockP()` unfold/fold pattern used by `PutUser`. Uses full
// `acc(s.LockP())` rather than the prior 1/2 fraction so the contract
// composes uniformly with the other discharged store methods on a sequential
// caller chain.
//
// Stream 3 Phase 4 sub-PR 3 (PutFollow + DeleteFollow): retires the
// `GhostPutFollow` and `GhostDeleteFollow` ghost stubs. Both methods are
// now their own proofs in `memstore.go`, sharing the same `LockP()`
// predicate footprint (PutFollow inserts into `s.follows`; DeleteFollow
// removes; both touch the same map field).
//
// Stream 3 Phase 4 sub-PR 4 (PutTweet): retires the `GhostPutTweet` ghost
// stub — `(*MemStore).PutTweet` is now its own proof in `memstore.go`. Same
// `LockP()` unfold/fold pattern as PutUser/PutFollow under the write lock.
// The slice append `s.byAuthor[t.Author] = append(...)` is quarantined into
// the tiny `// @ trusted` `appendTweet` shim. Postcondition is framing-only;
// F6 stays enforced at runtime by the explicit user-existence guard.
//
// Stream 3 Phase 4 sub-PR 5 (FollowSet): no ghost stub to retire (FollowSet
// never had one — the read-only contract was carried directly by the
// `// @ trusted` marker). `(*MemStore).FollowSet` is now its own proof in
// `memstore.go`, with the same `LockP()` unfold/fold pattern under `RLock`
// used by `HasUser`. The inner-map iteration over `s.follows[from]` is
// quarantined into the tiny `// @ trusted` `iterFollows` shim — same
// inner-map permission gap as `putFollowEdge` / `deleteFollowEdge`.
// Postcondition is framing-only.
//
// Stream 3 Phase 4 sub-PR 6 (HomeTimeline): retires the `GhostHomeTimeline`
// ghost stub. `(*MemStore).HomeTimeline` is now its own proof in
// `memstore.go` AT FRAMING LEVEL ONLY (`requires/ensures acc(s.LockP())`).
// Two tiny `// @ trusted` shims quarantine the inner operations:
// `gatherTimeline` (build the authors set from `follows[user]` and collect
// per-author tweet slices in one consolidated helper), and `sortTimeline`
// (the `sort.Slice` call with the F2 closure comparator). EXPLICIT
// NON-DISCHARGE: the F1 visibility postcondition (every returned tweet's
// author is in `{user} ∪ follows[user]`) and the F2 sort postcondition
// (returned list is sorted by (created_at desc, id desc)) are NOT formally
// verified here — both require quantifier reasoning out of scope for the
// per-method discharge cadence of S3P4. F2 in particular is blocked on a
// verified sort spec, tracked for the S3P6 stub-discharge follow-up stream.
// F1 stays enforced at runtime by the `authors` map construction; F2 by
// `sort.Slice` with the (CreatedAt desc, ID desc) less-function. Both are
// exercised end-to-end by the conformance suite.

package store

// LockP is the lock-invariant predicate for *MemStore. It abstracts the
// resource the mutex `mu` protects: write permission to the three internal
// maps. `mu` itself is a value-typed `sync.RWMutex`, and `stubs/sync` declares
// no permission tokens on `RWMutex`, so no field-permission for `mu` is asserted
// here. Mirrors the predicate body shapes in `clock.gobra` and `ids.gobra`.
pred (s *MemStore) LockP() {
	acc(&s.mu) &&
	acc(&s.users) && acc(s.users) &&
	acc(&s.follows) && acc(s.follows) &&
	acc(&s.byAuthor) && acc(s.byAuthor)
}

// (`GhostHomeTimeline` ghost stub retired by Stream 3 Phase 4 sub-PR 6 —
// `(*MemStore).HomeTimeline` is now its own proof in `memstore.go`,
// framing-only. F1 + F2 functional postconditions remain pending S3P6.)
